## STEP 2 — `SearchTextNormalizer` (pure Kotlin) + unit tests
New package `data/search/`. File `SearchTextNormalizer.kt`. No Android imports.

Why: the FTS tokenizer is `simple`: a token is a run of ASCII letters/digits/underscore or any
char >= 128, and it lowercases ASCII only. So WE must remove punctuation (Bengali danda `।`,
curly quotes, etc.), joiners and case, otherwise "খাই।" would be a different token from "খাই".

```kotlin
object SearchTextNormalizer {
    const val MIN_QUERY_CHARS = 2
    const val MAX_QUERY_TOKENS = 8

    /** Used for BOTH indexing and querying. Result: lowercase words separated by single spaces. */
    fun forIndex(raw: String): String {
        val nfc = java.text.Normalizer.normalize(raw, java.text.Normalizer.Form.NFC)
        val sb = StringBuilder(nfc.length)
        var lastWasSpace = true
        for (ch in nfc) {
            when {
                ch == '\u200D' || ch == '\u200C' -> Unit        // drop ZWJ/ZWNJ: keeps the word in one piece
                ch.isLetterOrDigit() || isMark(ch) -> {
                    sb.append(ch.lowercaseChar()); lastWasSpace = false
                }
                else -> if (!lastWasSpace) { sb.append(' '); lastWasSpace = true }
            }
        }
        return sb.toString().trimEnd()
    }

    private fun isMark(ch: Char): Boolean {
        val t = Character.getType(ch)
        return t == Character.NON_SPACING_MARK.toInt() ||
            t == Character.COMBINING_SPACING_MARK.toInt() ||
            t == Character.ENCLOSING_MARK.toInt()
    }

    /** FTS MATCH string, or null if the input is too short. Last token is a prefix search. */
    fun buildMatchQuery(userInput: String): String? {
        val norm = forIndex(userInput)
        if (norm.length < MIN_QUERY_CHARS) return null
        val tokens = norm.split(' ').filter { it.isNotEmpty() }.take(MAX_QUERY_TOKENS)
        if (tokens.isEmpty()) return null
        return tokens.mapIndexed { i, t -> if (i == tokens.lastIndex) "$t*" else t }.joinToString(" ")
    }
}
```
Bengali vowel signs, hasanta and anusvara are "marks", so `isMark` is REQUIRED. Do not remove it.
Tokens can only contain letters/digits/marks, so they can never contain FTS syntax characters.

Also add `PageRowId` (same file or neighbor):
```kotlin
object PageRowId {
    const val PAGES_PER_DOC = 1_000_000L
    fun of(docId: Long, pageIndex: Int): Long = docId * PAGES_PER_DOC + pageIndex
    fun docOf(rowId: Long): Long = rowId / PAGES_PER_DOC
    fun pageOf(rowId: Long): Int = (rowId % PAGES_PER_DOC).toInt()
    fun firstOf(docId: Long): Long = docId * PAGES_PER_DOC
    fun lastOf(docId: Long): Long = docId * PAGES_PER_DOC + PAGES_PER_DOC - 1
}
```

Unit tests `SearchTextNormalizerTest` (plain JUnit):
1. `forIndex("আমার সোনার বাংলা, আমি তোমায় ভালোবাসি।")` -> `"আমার সোনার বাংলা আমি তোমায় ভালোবাসি"`.
2. `forIndex("র\u200D্য")` contains neither `\u200D` nor `\u200C`.
3. `forIndex("Hello, World!")` -> `"hello world"`.
4. `forIndex("a_b")` -> `"a b"`.
5. `forIndex("১২৩ test")` -> `"১২৩ test"` (Bengali digits kept).
6. `forIndex("\u09C7\u09BE")` equals `forIndex("\u09CB")` (typing variants match).
