## STEP 5 — `SearchIndexer` (background text indexing)
In `data/search/`. Lives in `AppContainer` (lazy), uses `appScope`.

### 5a. `FileFingerprint`
```kotlin
object FileFingerprint {
    /** "<size>:<lastModified>" or null if the file cannot be read. */
    fun of(context: Context, uri: Uri): String?
}
```
- `file://` -> `File.length()` and `lastModified()`.
- `content://` -> `contentResolver.query(uri, null, null, null, null)`; read whichever of
  `OpenableColumns.SIZE`, `DocumentsContract.Document.COLUMN_LAST_MODIFIED`,
  `MediaStore.MediaColumns.DATE_MODIFIED` exist (use `getColumnIndex() >= 0`). If size is missing, use
  `openFileDescriptor(uri, "r")?.use { it.statSize }`. If nothing can be opened, return null.
Never throw.

### 5b. `IndexPolicy`
`fun canRunNow(context): PauseReason?` returns null when allowed, else
`PauseReason.LOW_BATTERY` (battery low AND not charging; read the sticky
`Intent.ACTION_BATTERY_CHANGED` with `registerReceiver(null, filter)`) or `PauseReason.POWER_SAVER`
(`PowerManager.isPowerSaveMode`). Constants in one object `IndexConfig`:
`MAX_PAGES_PER_DOC = 5000`, `BATCH_PAGES = 10`, `START_DELAY_MS = 3000`, `PAUSE_RECHECK_MS = 60_000`.

### 5c. Behavior
```kotlin
class SearchIndexer(
    private val appContext: Context, private val scope: CoroutineScope,
    private val repo: SearchIndexRepository, private val textEngine: PdfTextEngine,
    private val libraryCandidates: Flow<List<String>> /* uris, most recently opened first */
) {
    val pauseReason: StateFlow<PauseReason?>
    fun start()                         // idempotent; launches the collector and the worker
    fun prioritize(uri: String)         // put this uri at the FRONT of the queue (Reader opened it)
    suspend fun rebuildAll()            // repo.clearAll() then enqueue everything again
}
```
Implementation rules (keep it SIMPLE, do not over-engineer):
1. Queue = `ArrayDeque<String>` guarded by a `Mutex`, plus `Channel<Unit>(Channel.CONFLATED)` to wake
   the worker. One worker coroutine on `Dispatchers.Default`, processing ONE document at a time.
2. `start()`: launch (a) the collector: `delay(START_DELAY_MS)` first (do not slow the app start), then
   `libraryCandidates.collect { uris -> repo.pruneTo(uris.toSet()); enqueue the ones not DONE yet }`;
   (b) the worker loop.
3. Per document:
   - `fp = FileFingerprint.of(...) ?: return` (unreadable or missing file: skip, no status change).
   - `doc = repo.getOrCreate(uri, fp)`. If status is DONE, FAILED or ENCRYPTED -> return.
   - `textEngine.open(uri)`: `Failure(ENCRYPTED)` -> status ENCRYPTED; any other failure -> FAILED; return.
   - `repo.setPageCount`, status INDEXING.
   - Collect `session.pages(from = doc.nextPage)` while `pageIndex < min(pageCount, MAX_PAGES_PER_DOC)`.
     For each page: if `quality == GOOD` keep `pageIndex to SearchTextNormalizer.forIndex(text)`;
     otherwise keep nothing (EMPTY / GARBLED / LEGACY_BANGLA_FONT / FAILED pages get NO row; they are
     the OCR candidates later).
     Every `BATCH_PAGES` pages: `policy check` (see 4), then `repo.writeTextBatch(...)`.
     Flush the last partial batch. Then status DONE.
   - Always `session.close()` (use `.use {}`), also on cancellation.
   - A thrown exception for one document (not CancellationException) -> status FAILED, continue
     with the next document. One bad PDF must never stop the worker.
4. Before each batch: `while (policy.canRunNow(ctx) != null) { pauseReason.value = reason; delay(PAUSE_RECHECK_MS) }`,
   then `pauseReason.value = null`.
5. `yield()` between batches so the Text Mode requests (same PDFBox thread) are never starved.
6. `prioritize(uri)`: remove it from the queue if present and `addFirst`. If it is the document being
   processed right now, do nothing.

