- Run on a dedicated `Dispatchers.Default.limitedParallelism(1)`. Tesseract is NOT thread-safe.
- Result text: `SearchTextNormalizer.forIndex(TextNormalizer.clean(raw))`.

### 9e. `OcrRunner` (app-level, one document at a time)
```kotlin
sealed interface OcrState {
    data object Idle : OcrState
    data class Running(val uri: String, val page: Int, val total: Int) : OcrState
    data class Finished(val uri: String, val addedPages: Int) : OcrState
    data class Failed(val uri: String, val reason: OcrFailure) : OcrState   // NO_DATA, OPEN_FAILED, CANCELLED_LOW_BATTERY, OTHER
}
class OcrRunner(...) {
    val state: StateFlow<OcrState>
    fun start(uri: String)     // ignored if already running
    fun stop()
}
```
Algorithm for `start(uri)` (launch in `appScope`):
1. The doc must exist in the index with status DONE, else do nothing. `OcrEngine.open()` null -> `Failed(NO_DATA)`.
2. `have = repo.indexedPageSet(docId)`. Open ITS OWN `PdfRenderer` on its own file descriptor (do NOT use the
   shared renderer of `PdfEngine`; the Reader uses it). If `openFileDescriptor` is not seekable and
   `PdfRenderer` throws `IOException`, copy to `cacheDir/ocr_tmp/<hash>.pdf` and open that; delete the copy at the end.
   A password-protected PDF -> `Failed(OPEN_FAILED)`.
3. For `p in doc.ocrNextPage until doc.pageCount` (cap `IndexConfig.MAX_PAGES_PER_DOC`):
   - skip pages in `have`;
   - `ensureActive()`; policy check (`IndexPolicy`), if LOW_BATTERY -> `Failed(CANCELLED_LOW_BATTERY)` and stop
     (progress is saved, user can resume);
   - render: open page, scale = `RENDER_MAX_SIDE_PX / max(page.width, page.height)`, size = page size * scale,
     reduce while `w*h > RENDER_MAX_PIXELS`; `Bitmap.createBitmap(w, h, ARGB_8888)`, `eraseColor(PAGE_BACKGROUND)`
     (PdfRenderer renders on transparent, OCR needs white), `page.render(bmp, null, null, RENDER_MODE_FOR_PRINT)`;
     close the page in `finally`; `bmp.recycle()` after OCR. On `OutOfMemoryError`: retry ONCE at half size,
     then skip the page;
   - `result = session.recognize(bmp)`; if `result.meanConfidence >= MIN_CONFIDENCE` and text is not blank ->
     `repo.writeOcrPage(docId, p, text, ocrNextPage = p + 1)`; else just advance the pointer
     (`setOcrProgress`);
   - publish `Running(uri, p + 1, total)`.
4. At the end: `repo.finishOcr(docId)`, `Finished(uri, addedPages)`. Close session and renderer in `finally`.
5. Cancellation (`stop()` or scope cancel) must close everything and keep the saved pointer.

